-- title:
--   Height 4 from a rank-4 Cartier module and nilpotent [p]-coordinates
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ a perfect field of characteristic $p$. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $k$ in the sense of the structure [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormalModule.html#L170): a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $F$ over $k$ (given by two power series in $\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,2$ variables satisfying the usual normalisation and associativity), together with an action $a \mapsto X.\mathrm{act}(a)$ of $W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})$ by endomorphism pairs of $F$ and a pair $\varpi$, all of them law homomorphisms with vanishing constant coefficients, the action being multiplicative and additive for the group law, and $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi \circ \varpi = X.\mathrm{act}(p)$ and $\varpi \circ X.\mathrm{act}(a) = X.\mathrm{act}(\sigma a) \circ \varpi$ for the Witt Frobenius $\sigma$. Assume given a basis of the Cartier module $\mathrm{CartierModule}\,p\,X.F$ (tuples of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathbb{N}$, with zero constant coefficient, compatible with the Witt addition law and the group law) as a free $W(k)$-module indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,4$, and assume that for some $N$ both coordinates satisfy $X_i^N \in \bigl(X.\mathrm{act}(p)_0, X.\mathrm{act}(p)_1\bigr)$ in $k[[X_0,X_1]]$. The conclusion is $X.\mathrm{HasHeight}\,4$: the kernel algebra of the pair $X.\mathrm{act}(p)$ is a finite projective $k$-module and, for every field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $k \to \kappa$, the kernel algebra of the base-changed pair has $\kappa$-dimension $p^4$.
--
--   This is the computation of the height of a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over a perfect field of characteristic $p$ from Dieudonné-theoretic data: a Cartier module free of rank $4$ over $W(k)$ together with nilpotence of the coordinates modulo the ideal generated by multiplication by $p$ forces $X[p]$ to be finite locally free of rank $p^4$. It is used in the verification of height $4$ for the formal modules constructed from structure constants and edge constants in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_hasHeight_four_of_basis_cartierModule_of_X_pow_mem_span.lean

